        "preview": "---\nname: one-pager\ndescription: >-\n  Make a one-pager: one HTML page that shares an idea with teammates early,\n  or recaps work for them, with big pictures and little words.\ndisable-model-invocation: true\n---\n\nYou are making a one-pager: one HTML page to share with teammates. Usually it is an idea at an early stage, to get their first reactions; sometimes it is a recap of work done. The reader is new to the subject and has a minute.\n\nUse HTML to help them understand what we're discussing. Show them with big pictures and little words without withholding key details.\nUse your own taste, avoid lazy design, integrate real-world pictures/icons/visuals as needed but only selectively when it makes sense.\nWhen you do use prose/detail: Be clear, concise/terse, and avoid jargon. Explain things as if the viewer is new here, but don't use weird metaphors."
